# reviewed-binaries.sha256 — the pin manifest for every tracked binary asset.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# `CLAUDE.md`: "unreviewed binary assets must never be tracked". A binary cannot
# be reviewed in a diff — a reviewer sees `Binary files differ` and moves on, so
# a blob is the cheapest place in a repository to hide something. The reviewable
# substitute is a PIN: a binary may be tracked only if its digest appears here,
# which means adding or changing one requires editing this file in the same
# commit. That edit is visible, attributable, and shows up in review as a line
# someone had to type — which is exactly what the blob diff failed to be.
#
# Enforced by `scripts/publish.sh --check` (check D): a tracked binary missing
# from this manifest fails; a digest that no longer matches fails; a pin whose
# path is no longer tracked fails as stale bookkeeping.
#
# FORMAT — `shasum -a 256 -c` compatible: `<sha256>  <path>`
# To re-pin after a legitimate change:  shasum -a 256 <path>
#
# ── Documentation figures (mdBook, docs.noogram.org) ─────────────────────────
# Rendered from the TikZ sources beside them; light/dark pairs for the book
# theme. Reviewed as regenerated output of tracked source, not opaque input.
